---
title: Fennel Dauphinoise
description: A mild aniseed twist on the French bistro classic
source: https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/fennel-dauphinoise
author: Sara Buenfeld
image: https://images.immediate.co.uk/production/volatile/sites/30/2020/08/fennel-8563d2f.jpg?quality=90&webp=true&resize=440,400
course: Side
servings: 2
prep time: 15m
cook time: 1h
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: French
diet: Vegetarian
tags:
- vegetarian
- side-dish
- savoury
- french
---

Pre-heat oven to 160°C. Put the @potato{225%g}(very thinly sliced), @fennel{1%small bulb}(fronds reserved), @garlic{1%clove}(finely chopped), @whole milk{75%ml}, and @double cream{100%ml} into a #medium non-stick pan{}. Season well with @salt and @black pepper{}(freshly ground). Simmer gently, covered, for ~{10%minutes} until the potatoes are just tender. Stir halfway through.

Grease an #ovenproof dish{} with @margarine, add the mixture, and scatter with @parmesan{2%tbsp}(finely grated). Bake for ~{40%minutes} until the potatoes are golden and tender when pierced with a knife.

Snip the reserved fennel fronds over before serving.